<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Asbestos fence removal in Geelong nearly always starts the same way. A grey sheet in the back boundary fence cracks, a storm lifts one out, the mower clips the bottom edge again, or a renovation plan runs straight into a fence line nobody has looked at closely in forty years. If that fence went up between the mid 1940s and the late 1980s, asbestos cement is a fair assumption until a laboratory says otherwise. The good news is that the first step is cheap.</p><p>We do not hold an asbestos removal licence and we do not claim one. Removal is carried out by licensed asbestos removalists we work with, and their WorkSafe Victoria licence number appears on every quote. What we do is help you get the material identified properly and put you in touch with someone who can price the job, so you are comparing real quotes instead of guesses. If you are not certain what you are looking at, start with <a href="/asbestos-testing-geelong/">a test</a>, or call now on 0480 XXX XXX and talk it through first.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Handle</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">What's Included in Every Visit</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Get it tested before you touch it</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">A sample analysed by a NATA accredited laboratory is the only way to settle whether a fence is asbestos cement or plain concrete. Published Victorian rates run $88 to $160 per sample.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Fibro fencing is Class B work</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Asbestos cement sheeting is non-friable, which makes a fence Class B removal work in Victoria. Sheeting that has gone crumbly or been through a fire counts as friable, and friable material is always Class A.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Priced per sheet or per whole fence</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Published Victorian whole fence removal runs $1,000 to $3,500, and most quotes carry a minimum job charge of $800 to $1,500. If a quote is priced per linear metre, ask how that rate was worked out, because no reliable published figure exists.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Wrapped, labelled and taken to an authorised tip</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Sheets go into polythene about 200 microns thick, taped shut and marked with the asbestos warning label before they move. Only one landfill in the whole Barwon region is authorised to receive asbestos.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">The clearance certificate is the removalist's duty</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Above 10 square metres a clearance certificate is required, and where a homeowner engages the removalist directly, the licence holder has to obtain it. It comes from an independent person, so it shows up as a separate line at $165 to $250.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Geelong, the Bellarine, the Surf Coast and Colac</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Fence quotes across the post-war streets of Norlane and Corio, the older parts of Ocean Grove and Torquay, and out through Drysdale, Lara and Colac.</p>
      </div>
</div>
